# Task 04 Project Report
## Supervised Classification / Regression Modeling & Tuning

### 1. Objective
Build and compare at least four supervised classification models, optimize their hyperparameters with GridSearchCV and stratified 5-fold cross-validation, evaluate performance, and serialize the best model.

### 2. Dataset
The project uses the Wisconsin Diagnostic Breast Cancer dataset bundled with scikit-learn. It contains 569 observations and 30 numeric input features. The target is binary: malignant or benign. An 80/20 stratified train-test split was used (training: 455, test: 114).

### 3. Preprocessing and leakage prevention
Median imputation is included in every pipeline. Standard scaling is applied to Logistic Regression. All preprocessing is fitted within each cross-validation training fold because it is part of the scikit-learn Pipeline. This prevents validation/test information from influencing preprocessing.

### 4. Models and tuning
Four architectures were compared:
- Logistic Regression
- Random Forest
- Gradient Boosting
- Extra Trees

GridSearchCV used StratifiedKFold with 5 folds, shuffling, random_state=42, and ROC-AUC as the optimization metric.

### 5. Evaluation
The held-out test set was used to calculate accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, ROC-AUC, and the confusion matrix. The champion was selected using the highest mean cross-validation ROC-AUC.

Champion model: **Logistic Regression**

Best cross-validation ROC-AUC: **0.9959**

Test accuracy: **0.9825**

Test precision: **0.9861**

Test recall: **0.9861**

Test F1-score: **0.9861**

Test ROC-AUC: **0.9954**

Best parameters: `{'model__C': 1.0}`

### 6. Model comparison
| Model               |   Best CV ROC-AUC |   Test Accuracy |   Precision |   Recall |   F1-Score |   Test ROC-AUC |
|:--------------------|------------------:|----------------:|------------:|---------:|-----------:|---------------:|
| Logistic Regression |          0.995872 |        0.982456 |    0.986111 | 0.986111 |   0.986111 |       0.99537  |
| Extra Trees         |          0.994221 |        0.95614  |    0.958904 | 0.972222 |   0.965517 |       0.99289  |
| Gradient Boosting   |          0.992879 |        0.95614  |    0.946667 | 0.986111 |   0.965986 |       0.988757 |
| Random Forest       |          0.99226  |        0.947368 |    0.958333 | 0.958333 |   0.958333 |       0.993717 |

